+# ION Agent Branch Capsule Material Work Guard Protocol v0.1
+
+Status: active provisional protocol
+Created: 2026-05-11
+Authority: branch-capsule material-work preflight only
+Production authority: false
+Live execution authority: false
+
+## Purpose
+
+This protocol binds the branch-capsule doctrine to a concrete runtime guard for
+material work. It prevents a Codex worker or agent from beginning file-changing
+work unless the work is associated with a valid branch capsule and the requested
+write scope is declared inside that branch.
+
+This is an enforcement layer, not a settlement layer. It does not promote
+candidate branch output into shared Codex solo context.
+
+## Extends
+
+```text
+ION/02_architecture/ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
+ION/02_architecture/ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_BOOTSTRAP_BINDING_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
+ION/02_architecture/ION_MULTI_AGENT_CONTEXT_AND_WORKPACKET_SETTLEMENT_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
+```
+
+## Guard rule
+
+Before material work, the carrier should run or satisfy an equivalent
+`material_work_preflight` check:
+
+```text
+branch capsule present
+branch identity complete
+parent context proof loaded
+requested write scope declared by branch
+requested write scope does not touch shared Capsule/Mini/HOT_CONTEXT/STATUS/ROUTE
+requested write scope does not assign C-numbers
+requested write scope does not collide with another active branch claim
+settlement_required = true
+shared_context_write = false
+```
+
+If the guard fails, the worker must not proceed with material writes. It should
+create or repair a branch capsule, write a drift/blocker receipt if needed, and
+route the result through `context_settlement/inbox`.
+
+## Runtime helper
+
+The helper is:
+
+```text
+ION/04_packages/kernel/ion_agent_branch_capsule.py
+```
+
+The read-only preflight command is:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONPATH=ION/04_packages \
+python -m kernel.ion_agent_branch_capsule --ion-root . preflight \
+  --branch-record ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/<conversation>/<agent>/<task>/BRANCH_RECORD.json \
+  --write-scope ION/04_packages/kernel/example.py
+```
+
+Expected successful verdict:
+
+```text
+ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_READY
+```
+
+Expected blocked verdict:
+
+```text
+ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_BLOCKED
+```
+
+## Failure classes
+
+The guard can block for:
+
+```text
+branch_capsule_required_for_material_work
+branch_record_missing
+branch_record_invalid_json
+missing_required_field
+root_mismatch
+loaded_refs_missing_parent_context_proof
+shared_context_write_must_be_false
+settlement_required_must_be_true
+requested_write_scope_not_declared_in_branch
+requested_write_scope_shared_context_surface_forbidden
+requested_write_scope_checkpoint_assignment_surface_forbidden
+write_scope_overlap
+```
+
+## Non-claims
+
+This protocol does not:
+
+```text
+create branches automatically
+promote branch output
+update shared Capsule/Mini/HOT_CONTEXT/STATUS/ROUTE
+assign C-numbers
+run tests by itself
+reload services
+grant production authority
+grant live execution authority
+```
+
+## Next implementation lanes
+
+Future work may bind this guard into:
+
+```text
+Codex queue request validation
+agent invocation broker preflight
+ChatGPT Action Gateway validation
+JOC/dAimon cockpit branch panel
+context settler acceptance review
+```
+
+Those bindings must still preserve the settlement-only merge path.
